<v Maurice Chammah>In fact, Greg's already been accused pretty harshly of delaying David Wood's execution in all kinds of ways. In 2009, Wood was about to be put to death, and a day before it, Greg got them to delay by arguing that David Wood has an intellectual disability. The courts ultimately reject this appeal, but it takes five years for them to rule on it. Then they spend years arguing over evidence that was never DNA-tested. Last year, a judge, summarizing the last 15 years of this case, accused David's defense of a, quote, "pattern of piecemeal litigation and delay."
